# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Lyricist Pro — build-time configuration
#
# Copy to `.env` (or `.env.local`) to switch these on. EVERY ONE OF THEM IS
# READ AT BUILD TIME, not at run time: Vite substitutes the literal value into
# the bundle and Rollup then eliminates whatever the value makes unreachable.
# That is the mechanism, and it is why leaving a flag out does not merely
# disable a feature — it removes the code.
#
# `.env` is already covered by .gitignore. Do not commit one.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ── GHOST PILOT — INTERNAL MARKETING BUILD ONLY ─────────────────────────────
#
# The agentic UI robotics layer: the on-screen virtual cursor, the JSON command
# executor, synthetic DOM events, human-cadence typing, voice narration sync,
# and the OBS Studio WebSocket client. It exists so demo videos record
# themselves, hands-free, repeatably.
#
# ⚠ THIS MUST NEVER BE SET WHEN BUILDING A CUSTOMER INSTALLER.
#
# With it absent (or anything other than the exact string "true"), Rollup drops
# VirtualCursor.jsx, ghostPilot.js and obsClient.js from the graph entirely —
# no chunk is emitted, nothing is shipped dormant. Verified by grepping dist/
# for `localhost:4455` and `ghost-cursor`; both must be absent.
#
#   Record a demo:   VITE_FAFO_INTERNAL_BUILD=true npm run dev
#   Ship to a user:  npm run dist          (this line absent)
#
# Once running, drive it from the devtools console:
#   window.ghostPilot.run([
#     { action: 'obs_record_start' },
#     { action: 'speak', text: 'Here is The Matrix.', waitFor: 'play' },
#     { action: 'click', target: '[data-help*="semantic grid"]' },
#     { action: 'type',  target: '#ql-kw-input', text: 'neon rain, empty cup' },
#     { action: 'click', target: '[data-demo="ql-load"]' },
#     { action: 'wait',  ms: 800 },
#     { action: 'click', target: '[data-demo="matrix-autocraft"]' },
#     { action: 'speak', text: 'One press. Spread, lock, generate.', waitFor: 'end' },
#     { action: 'obs_record_stop' },
#   ])
#
# OBS needs Tools → WebSocket Server Settings enabled, on the default port
# 4455. If a password is set there, store it once in the browser:
#   localStorage.setItem('lyricist.obs.password', '<password>')
#
# VITE_FAFO_INTERNAL_BUILD=true


# ── PRODUCT ANALYTICS (PostHog) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Leave BOTH lines commented out and the build is telemetry-free in the literal
# sense: posthog-js is never pulled into the bundle graph, no chunk is emitted,
# no socket is opened, and the footer status deck reads "Air-Gapped Safe"
# because that is then true. The footer computes that claim from this flag
# rather than asserting it, so the two can never disagree.
#
# With a key set, the deck reads "Anonymous Usage Stats" instead and the
# tooltip says exactly what is collected.
#
# WHAT IS COLLECTED: tab_viewed, lattice_loaded, verse_generated,
# song_exported, stem_split_requested — plus counts, enum ids and booleans.
#
# WHAT IS NEVER COLLECTED: lyric text, keywords, prompts, model output, file
# names, file paths, audio, or API keys. Autocapture and session recording are
# both disabled explicitly (autocapture would otherwise record the contents of
# clicked elements and form fields, which in a lyrics editor is the user's
# song), and every event is filtered through a deny-list sanitiser on the way
# out. See src/services/analytics.js.
#
# VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# ── Modal (primary GPU backend for One Man Band) ─────────────────────────
# Modal runs the same ComfyUI + MiniMax-Music-3 the local engine runs, so a
# take made here matches one made on your desk. Deploy it once:
#
#   pip install modal
#   modal token new
#   modal secret create lyricist-comfy LYRICIST_TOKEN=<long-random-string>
#   modal run   modal/lyricist_comfy.py     # one-time 12 GB weight pull
#   modal deploy modal/lyricist_comfy.py    # prints your endpoint URL
#
# The endpoint is public, so the token is what stops a stranger running graphs
# on your GPU. Use a long random one and do not reuse it anywhere else.
VITE_MODAL_URL=
VITE_MODAL_TOKEN=

# Kaggle and Hugging Face are kept as optional fallbacks. Neither is required
# once Modal is deployed; leave them blank to hide them from the engine picker.
